* Lab coordinator – YooJeong Son (PhD student)
	Photo
	  

	One sentence
	 I'm studying K-12 students' reading comprehension across print, online, and AI-mediated environments, with a focus on designing interventions and examining the underlying psychological factors that influence their comprehension. 
	Research interests
	YooJeong was an elementary school teacher. Building on her experience, she is interested in bridging research and classroom practice by translating research findings into educational practices in K-12 settings. Her research mainly focuses on: 
* Content area literacy to build robust knowledge
* Online evaluation on multimodal and AI generated information
* Child-AI interaction during reading and writing
	Current project
	1. Knowledge revision: Read-Aloud Instruction for SciencE Learning (RAISE Learning)
2. Lateral reading intervention
3. Standards of Coherence: Measurement development studies
4. Supporting AI literacy within content-rich literacy instruction:  Content-rich Literacy and AI literacy via Project-based learning (CLAP).
5. Systematic review on digital reading comprehension
	Life outside work
	I enjoy spending time in nature and going camping.
	



































   * Yulu Sun (PhD student)
	Photo
	  

	One sentence
	My research focuses on bridging psychological research and educational practice to improve children’s reading and learning, particularly among children with developmental dyslexia.
	Research interests
	I aim to: (1) investigate the cognitive mechanisms that underlie reading and learning in both typical and atypical childhood development; (2) examine how literacy interactions with educational stakeholders shape children’s language and cognitive growth; (3) design and validate evidence-based, AI-enabled agents for school and home-based literacy assessments and interventions. 
	Current project
	1. Supporting inference-making using educational technology: Inference Galaxy
2. Systematic review on digital reading comprehension 


	Life outside work
	I enjoy hiking, reading novels and watching funny TV shows.
	





